{% extends 'base.twig' %}

{% block main_content %}

    <div class="row">
        <article class="content col-lg-9">
            <p class="text-muted"><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 28, 2026</p>

            <p>
                HuntRecipes is a family recipe website. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect,
                why we use it, when it may be shared, and the choices available to you when you use this website.
            </p>

            <h2>Information we collect</h2>

            <h3>Information you provide</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account information:</strong> your name, email address, sign-in identifier, and account status.</li>
                <li><strong>Profile information:</strong> information you add to your profile or chef profile, such as a photo, favorite foods, personal story, and cooking wisdom.</li>
                <li><strong>Recipe content:</strong> recipes, ingredients, instructions, photos, and other content you submit.</li>
                <li><strong>Activity:</strong> recipes you save as favorites and chef applications you submit.</li>
                <li><strong>Messages:</strong> your name, email address, and message when you use the contact form.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
            <p>
                When you visit HuntRecipes, our web server and service providers may receive technical information
                such as your IP address, browser and device type, requested pages, timestamps, and diagnostic or
                security logs. We use cookies and similar browser storage that are necessary to keep you signed in,
                protect forms, remember session state, and operate the website. HuntRecipes does not use advertising cookies.
            </p>

            <h2>How we use information</h2>
            <p>We use information to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>create and secure your account and authenticate sign-ins;</li>
                <li>display profiles, recipes, photos, favorites, and other requested features;</li>
                <li>review chef applications and administer the family recipe community;</li>
                <li>respond to questions and send service-related messages;</li>
                <li>maintain, troubleshoot, and protect HuntRecipes; and</li>
                <li>comply with applicable legal obligations and enforce our rights.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>When information is shared</h2>
            <p>
                We do not sell your personal information. We may share information with service providers that help
                us operate HuntRecipes, including Google Firebase for passwordless authentication, hosting and storage
                providers, and email delivery providers. These providers process information on our behalf or under
                their own applicable terms and privacy policies. We may also disclose information when required by law,
                to protect HuntRecipes or its users, or as part of a reorganization or transfer of the website.
            </p>

            <h2>Public content</h2>
            <p>
                Recipe content and chef profile information are intended to be shared with visitors and may be visible
                without signing in. Do not include sensitive personal information in recipes, photos, profile fields,
                or other content you choose to publish. Your favorites may be shown as part of your chef profile.
            </p>

            <h2>Data retention</h2>
            <p>
                We keep account information and contributed content while your account is active or while it is needed
                to operate the website. Contact messages, logs, backups, and other records may be retained for a reasonable
                period for support, security, recordkeeping, and legal purposes. Some information may remain in backups
                for a limited time after it is removed from the live website.
            </p>

            <h2>Your choices</h2>
            <p>
                You can review and update available profile information from your account page. You may also ask us to
                access, correct, or delete personal information associated with your account. Some information may be
                retained where reasonably necessary for security, legal compliance, dispute resolution, or enforcing agreements.
                To make a privacy request, please use our <a href="{{ route('contact') }}">contact form</a>. We may need
                to verify your identity before completing a request.
            </p>

            <h2>Security</h2>
            <p>
                We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards designed to protect personal information.
                HuntRecipes uses passwordless authentication and does not store your password. No method of transmission
                or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
            </p>

            <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
            <p>
                HuntRecipes is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information
                from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information, please contact us so
                we can review and, where appropriate, remove it.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy as HuntRecipes changes. We will post the revised policy on this page
                and update the effective date. Your continued use of the website after an update is subject to the revised policy.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact us</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions or requests about this Privacy Policy or your personal information, please use the
                <a href="{{ route('contact') }}">HuntRecipes contact form</a>.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>

{% endblock %}
